as did all of the food journey as well.

76
00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:08.700
So we were landlocked without really friends.

77
00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:11.900
We weren't really welcomed in Kauai by the community.

78
00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:13.730
And we found ourselves sort of

79
00:04:14.630 --> 00:04:18.320
staying in our three 30-foot yurts

80
00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.090
and I had a test kitchen

81
00:04:20.090 --> 00:04:23.100
and then I just started creating food,

82
00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:27.400
and that's most of the recipes in the plant power way.

83
00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:30.127
And then you were like, "I'm gonna go crazy.

84
00:04:30.127 --> 00:04:33.189
"We're starting a podcast."(laughs)

85
00:04:33.189 --> 00:04:34.540
I know.

86
00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:36.350
I mean, shout out to Chris Jabe,

87
00:04:36.350 --> 00:04:40.920
who invited us to live on his incredible property.

88
00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:41.873
Yes, Chris.

89
00:04:41.873 --> 00:04:43.110
Common ground, he since sold that property,

90
00:04:43.110 --> 00:04:46.940
but we were living, we've told the story many times,

91
00:04:46.940 --> 00:04:48.270
so I don't want to linger too long on it,

92
00:04:48.270 --> 00:04:51.460
but for those of you that are a little bit newer,

93
00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:55.220
we lived on this extraordinary property

94
00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:56.980
on the north shore of Kauai.

95
00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:59.730
It had been a mango farm,

96
00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:03.750
and Chris who owned it, was looking to figure out

97
00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:07.500
how to leverage this extraordinary place

98
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.620
for broader purposes.

99
00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:10.910
And for some reason,

100
00:05:10.910 --> 00:05:13.570
he thought that we could be helpful in that regard.

101
00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.220
Thank God he did, it was the first time--

102
00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:16.720
We were so broke at the time,

103
00:05:16.720 --> 00:05:17.780
he threw us a lifeline.

104
00:05:17.780 --> 00:05:19.670
He's like, come out to Kauai and live with me

105
00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.520
and we'll hang out and try to figure out what to do here.

106
00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.140
And we were like, okay.

107
00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:27.900
And before we knew it, like in a very short period of time,

108
00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.760
we had essentially relocated,

109
00:05:29.760 --> 00:05:31.370
thinking that we were gonna lose our house

110
00:05:31.370 --> 00:05:32.690
'cause we couldn't pay our bills,

111
00:05:32.690 --> 00:05:34.680
and he kept us afloat.

112
00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.550
And that became the crucible,

113
00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.580
like the incubator for so many beautiful things.

114
00:05:40.580 --> 00:05:45.400
And so, Really Chris J was very instrumental

115
00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.800
in the direction, the trajectory of our lives.

116
00:05:48.800 --> 00:05:53.800
It's unbelievable what an influence he had

117
00:05:53.990 --> 00:05:57.130
in ways that I'm sure he can barely appreciate

118
00:05:57.130 --> 00:05:59.580
in terms of being a catalyst

119
00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:01.980
for everything that we've birthed.

120
00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:05.460
And I think the lesson in there is that you never know,

121
00:06:05.460 --> 00:06:07.920
like people will come into your life

122
00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:12.120
and gently kind of nudge you in one direction or the other,

123
00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:14.763
that then over time,

124
00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:19.350
it only becomes evident like in the rear view mirror,

125
00:06:19.350 --> 00:06:21.840
like what an impact those people have.

126
00:06:21.840 --> 00:06:24.640
And I think we're all visited with

127
00:06:24.640 --> 00:06:27.560
some form or another of individuals like that.

128
00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:28.393
Makes a profound impact,

129
00:06:28.393 --> 00:06:30.091
but I think it's related to,

130
00:06:30.091 --> 00:06:31.750
I just want to tell a little bit more about that story,

131
00:06:31.750 --> 00:06:35.790
because it's very relevant to how I'm interacting

132
00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:38.270
with the creation of food right now.

133
00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:43.270
And at the point in time that Chris came into our lives,

134
00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:46.920
our house had been put in foreclosure,

135
00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:51.850
and I was sort of out of my ability to stall anymore.

136
00:06:51.850 --> 00:06:53.830
And I was very devastated,

137
00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.420
came home and told all you guys,

138
00:06:55.420 --> 00:06:56.823
I was like we're gonna lose the house,

139
00:06:56.823 --> 00:06:59.250
in like 30 days it's gonna be gone.

140
00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:01.390
So I came home and I was just,

141
00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:05.460
I had one of those moments of feeling sort of lost

142
00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:08.430
and disconnected from spirituality and God

143
00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.000
and like, how could this be happening?

144
00:07:11.000 --> 00:07:13.870
And I remember a Saul David Raye,

145
00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:17.230
who's an amazing yoga teacher in the LA area,

146
00:07:17.230 --> 00:07:20.110
he reached out and he hired me.

147
00:07:20.110 --> 00:07:23.620
He said, "SriMati, will you cook for my Thai yoga retreat?"

148
00:07:23.620 --> 00:07:26.596
And he said, you know, "I can pay you pretty well."

149
00:07:26.596 --> 00:07:28.910
And so I remember leaving, and I just told you,

150
00:07:28.910 --> 00:07:30.417
I said, "There is no way

151
00:07:30.417 --> 00:07:32.627
"that we are being moved out of this house

152
00:07:32.627 --> 00:07:35.027
"without an opportunity.

153
00:07:35.027 --> 00:07:37.287
"It's impossible with the amount of heart

154
00:07:37.287 --> 00:07:39.567
"and presence and how much we had gone through

155
00:07:39.567 --> 00:07:41.457
"and how bonded we were and committed

156
00:07:41.457 --> 00:07:43.830
"to really serving our heart."

157
00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.580
And so I remember going up there

158
00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.300
just feeling completely in a state of,

159
00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:50.660
I don't know, like I just don't know anything,

160
00:07:50.660 --> 00:07:51.970
like if this is happening,

161
00:07:51.970 --> 00:07:54.923
I was downing all of my instincts.

162
00:07:56.344 --> 00:07:58.700
And so I just decided to literally

163
00:07:58.700 --> 00:08:01.230
put all of my energy into preparing food

164
00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:02.790
for this Thai yoga retreat.

165
00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:07.790
And I, maybe one of the few times that I was single focus

166
00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:10.610
because I do so many things,

167
00:08:10.610 --> 00:08:15.610
but I really stepped into this as a sort of Seva service.

168
00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:17.900
And the food became activated

169
00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:22.210
with something that was beyond my ability to create food.

170
00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:25.920
And I had people weeping when they were eating my pie

171
00:08:25.920 --> 00:08:27.800
and they were leaving Saul's retreat

172
00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.320
to stay with me in the kitchen.

173
00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:31.067
And he was joking with me saying like,

174
00:08:31.067 --> 00:08:33.037
"What are you doing to my students?

175
00:08:33.037 --> 00:08:34.920
"Like they just want to be with you."

176
00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:38.377
And so I remember he was very generously said,

177
00:08:38.377 --> 00:08:41.960
"Please invite Rich and the kids up to the final dinner."

178
00:08:41.960 --> 00:08:43.610
And I remember you walked in,

179
00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:48.610
it was up at Bill's place up in Santa Barbara.

180
00:08:50.010 --> 00:08:50.910
Casa Blanca?

181
00:08:50.910 --> 00:08:51.743
No, that's not it.

182
00:08:51.743 --> 00:08:52.990
Casa Barranca, that was it.

183
00:08:52.990 --> 00:08:54.518
Yeah, yeah, I remember that very well.

184
00:08:54.518 --> 00:08:55.557
Yeah, remember that place,

185
00:08:55.557 --> 00:09:00.557
it was like a really cool sort of art deco sort of place.

186
00:09:01.620 --> 00:09:02.610
Anyway.

187
00:09:02.610 --> 00:09:06.060
And you walked in and you said, have you read your emails?

188
00:09:06.060 --> 00:09:07.080
And I said, no.

189
00:09:07.080 --> 00:09:09.160
And you said, go read your email right now.

190
00:09:09.160 --> 00:09:10.740
And I went and read my email.

191
00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:13.520
And Chris J had replied to an email

192
00:09:13.520 --> 00:09:16.270
that I had sent him two years prior.

193
00:09:16.270 --> 00:09:18.870
And he said, I want to speak to you and Rich

194
00:09:18.870 --> 00:09:20.150
I'm halfway through the book

195
00:09:20.150 --> 00:09:21.040
and we wanna meet.

196
00:09:21.040 --> 00:09:24.450
And 10 days later, he was sitting in our living room

197
00:09:24.450 --> 00:09:26.870
having a meeting with all of us.

198
00:09:26.870 --> 00:09:31.180
So it was a very sort of profound demonstration

199
00:09:31.180 --> 00:09:36.180
about how, when you step into devotion at that level

200
00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:41.370
and abandon your personalities, ideas and trajectories,

201
00:09:41.640 --> 00:09:45.022
just how beautiful life can be.

202
00:09:45.022 --> 00:09:48.853
Yeah there's many layers to this idea of surrender, right?

203
00:09:48.853 --> 00:09:51.989
So one of the lines in finding Ultra is

204
00:09:51.989 --> 00:09:52.860
that when your heart is true,

205
00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:55.590
the universe will conspire to support you.

206
00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:56.940
And I believe that,

207
00:09:56.940 --> 00:09:59.900
and I've seen that play out in so many people's lives.

208
00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.620
And I felt like when I put finding ultra out

209
00:10:02.620 --> 00:10:05.840
that my heart was true and the universe would conspire

210
00:10:05.840 --> 00:10:10.557
to somehow figure out a way to support us in this mission

211
00:10:11.940 --> 00:10:14.000
and nothing was happening, right?

212
00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.710
The phone was not ringing.

213
00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.490
There was no money coming in.

214
00:10:17.490 --> 00:10:19.620
We were unable to pay our bills.

215
00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:21.540
And when Saul called you,

216
00:10:21.540 --> 00:10:23.750
it was like, yes, I will do that.

217
00:10:23.750 --> 00:10:25.270
Like, I'll do anything.

218
00:10:25.270 --> 00:10:27.740
And when Chris said, come out to Kauai,

219
00:10:27.740 --> 00:10:29.960
we said, yes, we had no other options.

220
00:10:29.960 --> 00:10:31.610
But also it was like, okay,

221
00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:34.920
we're just giving ourselves over to work wherever

222
00:10:34.920 --> 00:10:36.670
and however we're being directed.

223
00:10:36.670 --> 00:10:40.520
And I just remember moving into those yurts on this farm

224
00:10:40.520 --> 00:10:42.860
and thinking like, we may never see our house again

225
00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:46.333
and perhaps we're just gonna be living in these yurts now.

226
00:10:46.333 --> 00:10:47.690
(laughing)

227
00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:50.300
Like that's it, like now we live in Kauai,

228
00:10:50.300 --> 00:10:52.540
you know, I don't know what's gonna happen tomorrow.

229
00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.870
Like this sense of completely letting go

230
00:10:55.870 --> 00:11:00.420
of any idea or attachment to

231
00:11:00.420 --> 00:11:04.040
your sense of expectations or outcomes,

232
00:11:04.040 --> 00:11:08.280
but that is a practice of devotion in and of itself right?

233
00:11:08.280 --> 00:11:09.630
We could've never known

234
00:11:09.630 --> 00:11:11.830
that that would be a trigger point

235
00:11:11.830 --> 00:11:13.610
to lead us in these other directions.

236
00:11:13.610 --> 00:11:16.000
And certainly I would've preferred

237
00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:18.200
the timeline to look differently.

238
00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:21.380
And I had no, like, it wasn't my plan,

239
00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:22.213
I don't know about you,

240
00:11:22.213 --> 00:11:23.530
that we were gonna go live in yurts.

241
00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:25.670
Like I had a whole other agenda and idea

242
00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:26.890
of how this would play out,

243
00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:31.690
but the letting go, which feels like giving up

244
00:11:31.690 --> 00:11:35.367
is really an act of strength.

245
00:11:35.367 --> 00:11:40.140
And so reframing how you approach setbacks and obstacles

246
00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:45.370
is I think a really instructive lesson

247
00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:48.420
that helps me even now, when we face obstacles

248
00:11:48.420 --> 00:11:50.680
or things aren't going the way that we would like

249
00:11:50.680 --> 00:11:54.140
to just be like present with what is happening

250
00:11:55.114 --> 00:11:59.520
and detached from the direction that it's leading you,

251
00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:02.100
because you simply do not know.

252
00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:04.920
Yeah and when the adversity or the constriction

253
00:12:04.920 --> 00:12:06.950
it's like you felt you were going crazy,

254
00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:08.620
you were like, I got to get off this island.

255
00:12:08.620 --> 00:12:09.920
I'm gonna go crazy, like I hate it.

256
00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:12.410
Well, first of all let me just say, like, it's beautiful

257
00:12:12.410 --> 00:12:13.625
and I love, there's a lot of great

258
00:12:13.625 --> 00:12:16.497
I don't wanna be like panning Kauai,

259
00:12:16.497 --> 00:12:19.080
but it was challenging.
We loved Kauai.

260
00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.080
Yes, because we were far away from our friends.

261
00:12:22.080 --> 00:12:23.900
We were in a new place.

262
00:12:23.900 --> 00:12:24.970
